  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Catalysing Policy Reform for a Just Rural Transition</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agriculture is vital for food security, livelihoods and national incomes. It is highly vulnerable to climate change and environmental damage; meanwhile it is a key driver of climate change, nature loss water use and contamination. Policy reform is key to achieving sustainable agricultural systems. This programme will catalyse policy reform in 4-5 developing countries, achieve progress and maintain momentum on repurposing harmful and inefficient subsidies to achieve more sustainable, equitable outcomes. Through additional support to an existing partnership between the UK and the World Bank, it will support countries to move from the successfully completed analysis stage to trialling policy reform by delivering the preparation activities and operational plans required to progress to implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
